Z||000000||p-man||10-18-2000||08:11 PM|||| I was wondering besides the intake being different to add the blower to the 3800 motor to make a monster.what else would be neeed to add the blower to the naturally aspirated version of the 3800? all the specs. are the same for the interals right? i know a oil cooler would need to be added and a new PCM or chip to compensate for the blower needing more fuel, air ,ETC. IF you know anything about this please reply or list websites that could help me alittle.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||10-18-2000||08:44 PM||||You'll definatly need to reprogram the ECM. Just what that means depends on which ECM it is. (Stock Fiero V6 ECM would need a chip. Some newer GM computers hook up to a PC or other programming tool.)<P>depending on just how it's setup now you may also need a diferant MAP sensor. Most boosted applications need a 2 atmosphere MAP. (3 ATM for high boost.) The stock ones are often only 1 ATM. <P>You'll also need work on the fuel system. The best solution is a boost compensated fuel regulator. As boost rises fuel rail pressure rises to compensate. Some systems do this by replacing the stock one others add a second regulator.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||10-18-2000||09:09 PM||||The intake and all accessories mounting are different. Depending on the year, the cranks and rods and pistons are different, but that's not a show-stopper.<P>The 92-95 don't use a map sensor (except for the boost gauge). All 92-2000 use a mass air flow sensor. The map is backup. Boost is limited by the pulley. <P>The ECM's are the same, but the calibration is different.<P>Frankly, start with an SC engine. By the time you scrounge everything, you'll wish you had. If you can afford the blower, you can afford the whole engine.<P>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wannabe||10-19-2000||12:26 AM||||The heads are also different in that the SC heads are machined to accept the fuel injectors in the head, while the n/a engines have the injectors in the intake manifold. N/a heads can be modified to accept the injectors.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dan86gt3.8||10-19-2000||10:41 AM||||I have also wondered that myself many times...  but got stick with n/a till I graduate||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||10-19-2000||11:38 AM||||The heads are different between te NA and SC only in the 96 and up Series II. The injectors are in the intake on both NA and SC Series I engines. The M-62 blower is not as wide as the M-90.<P>Start looking for a real SC engine.||||reg||1
